{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.97,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["Q6", "U38"],
      "pins": ["Q6.2", "Q6.3", "U38.1", "U38.6"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0110"],
      "observed": "Q6's source (pin 2) is on +5V and its drain (pin 3) is on NET0110, which also carries USB-C VBUS and U38 VIN. U38 SENSE (pin 6) is on +5V.",
      "expected": "For the intended LTC4412 P-channel ideal-diode path, the MOSFET should be oriented with its source on the input/VBUS side and its drain on the system +5V side, consistent with the controller's input and output sense connections.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\")) (name \"+5V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q6\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\")) (node (ref \"U38\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VIN\")) (name \"NET0110\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U38\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"SENSE\")) (name \"+5V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "\"USB power-path controller intended to OR/protect a USB power input\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The reversed MOSFET orientation undermines the intended ideal-diode path: USB input may not supply the system rail correctly, and the body-diode direction can permit reverse current from the system rail toward USB VBUS.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R62"],
      "pins": ["R62.1", "R62.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "The schematic value is 24k and the SPICE deck models 24k, but R62's listed MPN is FRC0805J240TSD and its description says 24Ω.",
      "expected": "The resistor value and sourcing metadata should agree. If 24k is intended, the listed MPN/description should specify 24k; if the listed MPN is procured, the design value should reflect 24Ω and its effect on the output should be checked.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R62\") (value \"24k\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±1% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R62 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is used for assembly, R62 would be about 1000 times lower than the simulated/design value and could heavily load the VOUTP-to-VOUTN output, potentially causing excessive current or supply collapse.",
      "confidence": 0.89
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: Q6 is oriented opposite to the input-to-system ideal-diode path indicated by the LTC4412 connections. R62 also has a 24k schematic/SPICE value but sourcing metadata for a 24Ω part, creating a potentially consequential assembly mismatch."
}

